Krammer wrote:
> Well, I would like the Master Key of Thievery, but I've heard that
> wishing for an artifact has a high probability of failure. So I'm
> hesitant to use a wish on potentially nothing. How useful is the Key's
> half damage? Is it worth wasting a couple of wishes to acquire it?

With 8 wishes to spare, you should go for it. (Assuming you're
chaotic; otherwise try to get the Orb of Fate as Janis suggested.)
Even if 6 artifacts have already been generated, you've still got
a 74% chance of getting one if you spend 4 wishes.  If you've seen
a *lot* of artifacts it's still kind of risky.  If there have been
10 generated, then you've only got a 55% chance of getting a new one
in 4 wishes for example.

As for the rest, a magic marker is never a wasted wish, especially
as a wizard since you've got a good chance of writing and using a
+polymorph.  And be sure to save at least one non-wrest wish for
a cockatrice corpse on Astral.  There's just no substitute for dealing
with the hoards up there, especially with the Amulet draining your
power whenever you cast a spell.  With a rubber chicken, you can save
that power for casting finger of death on Famine and Pestilence.


